{
 "total": 32.19,
 "planned": false,
 "beats": [
  {
   "text": "This animal is named after a monster with snakes for hair.",
   "visual": "hook",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.12
  },
  {
   "text": "It's a basket star.",
   "visual": "name",
   "start": 3.12,
   "end": 4.389
  },
  {
   "text": "Its scientific name means Gorgon's head, like Medusa.",
   "visual": "name",
   "start": 4.389,
   "end": 7.543
  },
  {
   "text": "Its five arms split again and again into tiny branches.",
   "visual": "branch",
   "start": 7.543,
   "end": 10.662
  },
  {
   "text": "To eat, it opens them into the current.",
   "visual": "open",
   "start": 10.662,
   "end": 12.449
  },
  {
   "text": "They form a bowl-shaped net.",
   "visual": "open",
   "start": 12.449,
   "end": 14.087
  },
  {
   "text": "Tiny animals drift into it.",
   "visual": "drift",
   "start": 14.087,
   "end": 15.806
  },
  {
   "text": "The branches are covered in microscopic hooks.",
   "visual": "hooks",
   "start": 15.806,
   "end": 18.458
  },
  {
   "text": "They grab the prey like a cat's claws.",
   "visual": "hooks",
   "start": 18.458,
   "end": 20.768
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the tips curl around it in a knot.",
   "visual": "knot",
   "start": 20.768,
   "end": 22.728
  },
  {
   "text": "And the arm rolls the food to its mouth.",
   "visual": "mouth",
   "start": 22.728,
   "end": 25.079
  },
  {
   "text": "It can be more than half a meter wide.",
   "visual": "size",
   "start": 25.079,
   "end": 27.134
  },
  {
   "text": "No wonder it's named after Medusa.",
   "visual": "medusa",
   "start": 27.134,
   "end": 29.159
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow BioNiche for more weird animals.",
   "visual": "cta",
   "start": 29.159,
   "end": 32.19
  }
 ],
